 {
   "id": "grammar.b2.28.02.marcadores-digresion",
-  "title": "Discourse Markers of Digression & Incidental Remarks",
+  "title": "Side Remarks and Coming Back",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Los marcadores de digresión introducen un comentario lateral, una precisión secundaria o una observación tangencial que se desvía momentáneamente del hilo conductor principal del texto sin que se pierda la cohesión global."
+      "content": "Sometimes you want to add something that is not part of your main line: a detail that has just come to mind, or a comment on the side. Spanish has set phrases that tell the listener \"this is a side remark\", and one that tells them \"now I am back\". *Por cierto* (\"by the way\") brings in a new thought loosely connected to what you were saying. *A propósito* also means \"by the way\", and *a propósito de* + noun means \"speaking of\": the remark is triggered by something just mentioned. *Dicho sea de paso* (\"incidentally\", literally \"said in passing\") fits a short comment, often between commas inside a sentence. To go back, use *volviendo a lo que decíamos* (\"going back to what we were saying\")."
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Marcadores de digresión en prosa formal",
+      "title": "Side remarks and the way back",
       "rows": [
         [
-          "El proyecto fue aprobado en mayo; por cierto, con el apoyo de todas las bancadas.",
-          "The project was approved in May; by the way, with the support of all factions."
+          "Mañana tengo una reunión. Por cierto, ¿tienes el informe?",
+          "I have a meeting tomorrow. By the way, do you have the report?"
         ],
         [
-          "A propósito de la reforma tributaria, los gremios presentaron una contrapropuesta.",
-          "Speaking of tax reform, the labor unions presented a counterproposal."
+          "A propósito, ¿ya compraste los boletos?",
+          "By the way, have you already bought the tickets?"
         ],
         [
-          "El informe omite, dicho sea de paso, el impacto sobre las comunidades ribereñas.",
-          "The report omits, by the way, the impact on riverside communities."
+          "A propósito de la reunión, ¿a qué hora empieza?",
+          "Speaking of the meeting, what time does it start?"
         ],
         [
-          "Conviene señalar, entre paréntesis, que la vigencia del tratado expira en 2030.",
-          "It is worth pointing out, parenthetically, that the treaty expires in 2030."
+          "La oficina, dicho sea de paso, está muy cerca de mi casa.",
+          "The office, incidentally, is very close to my house."
+        ],
+        [
+          "Volviendo a lo que decíamos, ¿quién presenta el informe?",
+          "Going back to what we were saying, who presents the report?"
         ]
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Evita el abuso de digresiones en textos ensayísticos: 'dicho sea de paso' debe emplearse de forma mesurada para enriquecer el argumento sin dispersar la atención del lector."
+      "content": "A side remark is short, and you should come back to the main line afterwards. You know *además* from A2 Unit 28: use it, not these phrases, to add a main point. *Volviendo* is the gerund of *volver*, and *decíamos* is the *imperfecto* of *decir* with *nosotros*."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-03-a-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-03-a-gr.json
index 1d545f76..ff46b297 100644
--- a/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-03-a-gr.json
+++ b/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-03-a-gr.json
@@ -1,36 +1,32 @@
 {
   "id": "grammar.b2.28.03.marcadores-continuidad",
-  "title": "Discourse Markers of Continuity & Thematic Transition",
+  "title": "Moving On and Picking Up a Topic",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Los marcadores de continuidad y progresión temática aseguran que el discurso avance fluidamente entre un punto ya establecido y el siguiente razonamiento deductivo o explicativo. Señalan la reanudación del argumento central o una reformulación estratégica."
+      "content": "You know *en cuanto* (\"as soon as\") from A2 Unit 27 and *además* from A2 Unit 28. This lesson adds three phrases that keep a talk moving. *Pues bien* (\"well then\", \"right\") closes what you have just said and moves on to the next step. *En cuanto a* (\"as for\") picks out one topic from several and comments on it. *Por lo que se refiere a* (\"as far as ... is concerned\") does the same job and sounds more formal. With these phrases you can go through a list of topics one by one."
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Marcadores de progresión y transición",
+      "title": "Three ways to keep a talk moving",
       "rows": [
         [
-          "Pues bien, examinadas las pruebas periciales, el tribunal absolvió al inculpado.",
-          "Now then, having examined the expert evidence, the court acquitted the defendant."
+          "Pues bien, ya conocemos el problema; ahora busquemos una solución.",
+          "Well then, we now know the problem; now let us look for a solution."
         ],
         [
-          "Dicho esto, no debemos soslayar las dificultades presupuestarias que persisten.",
-          "Having said this, we must not sidestep the budgetary difficulties that remain."
+          "En cuanto a la comida, yo me ocupo.",
+          "As for the food, I will take care of it."
         ],
         [
-          "Así las cosas, el parlamento se vio forzado a negociar un texto de consenso.",
-          "As things stood, parliament was forced to negotiate a consensus text."
-        ],
-        [
-          "Ahora bien, la viabilidad financiera exige un estricto control de gasto público.",
-          "Now, financial viability demands strict control of public spending."
+          "Por lo que se refiere al transporte, hay un autobús cada hora.",
+          "As far as transport is concerned, there is a bus every hour."
         ]
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "'Pues bien' y 'así las cosas' exigen coma inmediatamente posterior. Marcan una pausa deliberada en la que el orador o ensayista evalúa el escenario construido antes de dar el siguiente paso."
+      "content": "After *en cuanto a* and *por lo que se refiere a* comes a noun phrase: *en cuanto a la comida*, *en cuanto al transporte* (*a* + *el* = *al*). With a verb, *en cuanto* alone means \"as soon as\" and takes the subjunctive for the future: *En cuanto llegues, llámame*. Do not confuse the two."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-04-a-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b2/b2-28-04-a-gr.json
